@startuml SPECS-Use-Case
title SPECS PC Configuration and Optimization Platform\nHigh-Level UML Use Case Diagram

left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam actorStyle awesome
skinparam usecase {
  BackgroundColor #F7FBFF
  BorderColor #245B78
  ArrowColor #245B78
}

actor "PC Builder /\nVisitor" as User
actor "Registered\nUser" as Member
actor Administrator as Admin
actor "Component Catalog &\nPricing Data" as Catalog <<external system>>
actor "Authentication\nService" as Auth <<external system>>
actor "Natural-Language\nService" as NLP <<external system>>

Member --|> User

rectangle "SPECS System" {
  usecase "Browse, Search, and\nFilter Components" as UC_Browse
  usecase "Create or Edit\nPC Build" as UC_Create
  usecase "Calculate Total\nBuild Cost" as UC_Cost
  usecase "Evaluate Component\nCompatibility" as UC_Compat
  usecase "Explain Incompatibility\nand Affected Components" as UC_Explain
  usecase "Recommend Compatible\nReplacement" as UC_Replace
  usecase "Specify Budget, Workload,\nand Build Preferences" as UC_Requirements
  usecase "Generate Optimized\nPC Build" as UC_Optimize
  usecase "Explain Component\nSelection Reasons" as UC_Reasons
  usecase "Modify Generated Build\nand Recheck Compatibility" as UC_Modify
  usecase "Compare PC Builds" as UC_Compare
  usecase "Save, Rename, Duplicate,\nUpdate, or Delete Build" as UC_Manage
  usecase "Share Read-Only\nBuild Link" as UC_Share
  usecase "Manage Component Records,\nCompatibility Rules, and Scores" as UC_Admin
  usecase "Authenticate User" as UC_Auth
  usecase "Interpret Natural-Language\nBuild Request" as UC_NLP
}

User --> UC_Browse
User --> UC_Create
User --> UC_Optimize
User --> UC_Compare
User --> UC_Modify
Member --> UC_Manage
Member --> UC_Share
Member --> UC_Auth
Admin --> UC_Admin
Admin --> UC_Auth

UC_Create .> UC_Cost : <<include>>
UC_Create .> UC_Compat : <<include>>
UC_Compat .> UC_Explain : <<extend>>
UC_Explain .> UC_Replace : <<extend>>
UC_Optimize .> UC_Requirements : <<include>>
UC_Optimize .> UC_Compat : <<include>>
UC_Optimize .> UC_Cost : <<include>>
UC_Optimize .> UC_Reasons : <<include>>
UC_Modify .> UC_Compat : <<include>>
UC_Modify .> UC_Cost : <<include>>
UC_Manage .> UC_Auth : <<include>>
UC_Share .> UC_Auth : <<include>>
UC_NLP .> UC_Requirements : <<extend>>
UC_Optimize .> UC_NLP : <<extend>>

Catalog --> UC_Browse
Catalog --> UC_Cost
Catalog --> UC_Compat
Catalog --> UC_Optimize
Auth --> UC_Auth
NLP --> UC_NLP

note right of NLP
  Optional/stretch integration.
  Any resulting build is still
  validated by SPECS rules.
end note

@enduml
